Patch 70 -- p72: phases A+B+C as one native root, plus the routed shader frontend
and the GL-work census.

Three things that belong together because they were built together:

1. mgs2_draw_state_abc_body() is one contiguous transaction -- resource/stream
   preload, the whole dirty-state loop including its bitmap clear, and the
   resource/UAV bindings with FBO validation -- behind the marked entry
   mgs2_draw_state_abc_island() (id 0x29). Shader phase D stays guest, which is
   the entire difference from the rejected p71.
2. shader_generate_code() called the shader FRONTEND vtable at four sites that
   nothing routed; native ARM would have branched to a guest x86 pointer on any
   FFP shader cache miss inside a native root. They now dispatch through the new
   MGS2_P50_SHADER_FRONTEND site (MGS2_P50_SITES 36 -> 37).
3. MGS2_GL_CENSUS counts what the driver is actually asked to do, by family. The
   profile puts 42.5% of user cycles inside libmali, which porting cannot remove.
   Compiles away entirely when the define is absent.

MGS2_FUSED_ABC_AB selects the symmetric A/B build; without it the root is always
routed, which is the p72c candidate. Correctness, A/B and soak are in sections
14.2 to 14.6 of the brief.

